{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This article describes how KeyboardKit can identify and open host applications."}],"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationResolver"],"anchor":"Types"},{"title":"Views","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationPicker"],"anchor":"Views"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"role":"article","images":[{"identifier":"Feature-Host.jpg","type":"card"}],"title":"Host Application"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host application is the application that is using your keyboard. Being able to identify the host application is important for keyboards that should customize themselves for certain apps, or navigate back from the main app after certain tasks.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"👑 KeyboardKit Pro unlocks host application features for all licenses that include the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/ProFeature\/hostApplication"},{"type":"text","text":" feature. You can sign up for KeyboardKit Pro from the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/keyboardkit.com"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" has ways to identify the host application. However, since the standard way of resolving this information normally involves accessing system APIs, it’s not included in KeyboardKit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit therefore defines an abstract "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationResolver"},{"type":"text","text":" function and lets us fill it in with a plugin. This isolates the system APIs usage to the plugin, and lets you choose whether to use it or not."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Plugin","anchor":"Plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit has a KeyboardKitHostPlugin that defines a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationResolver","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that resolves the host application through the use of certain system APIs. The reason for this separation is to avoid having system API usages in KeyboardKit.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" article for information on how to use this plugin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Resolving the Host Application","type":"heading","anchor":"Resolving-the-Host-Application"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you have set up a resolver, you will be able to use controller functions like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController\/resolveHostApplicationBundleId(pollingInterval:timeout:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController\/resolveHostApplication(pollingInterval:timeout:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", etc. to resolve host app information."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext\/hostApplicationBundleId"},{"type":"text","text":" is automatically set when you call these functions. It’s persisted (provided that you have enabled "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing"},{"type":"text","text":") to let you access it from the main app, and is automatically reset when the keyboard is restarted."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit Pro unlocks a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" enum that defines known applications that can be opened with deep links:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"App Store, Apple Books, Apple Calendar, Apple Clock, Apple FaceTime, Apple Files, Apple Find My, Apple Health, Apple Home, Apple Mail, Apple Maps, Apple Messages, Apple Music, Apple Music Classical, Apple News, Apple Notes, Apple Photos, Apple Podcasts, Apple Reminders, Apple Safari, Apple Shortcuts, Apple Stocks, Apple TV, Apple Wallet, Apple Weather, Airbnb, Amazon Prime, Amazon Shopping, Audible, Bambu Handy, Bear, Bloomberg, Blue Sky, Brave, Bolt, ChatGPT, CityMapper, Claude, Day One, Discord, Disney+, DoorDash, Drafts, Dropbox, DuckDuckGo, Duolingo, Evernote, Facebook, Firefox, Gemini, GitHub, Gmail, Google Assistant, Google Calendar, Google Chrome, Google Docs, Google Drive, Google Home, Google Maps, Google Photos, Google, Google Sheets, Google Slides, Google Translate, Hulu, Instagram, Ivory, KakaoTalk, KeyboardKit Demo, Kindle, LINE, LinkedIn, Lyft, Mastodon, Meetup, Messenger, Microsoft Edge, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft OneDrive, Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft PowerPoint, Microsoft Teams, Microsoft Word, Netflix, Notion, Obsidian, 1Password, Overcast, Pinterest, Pocket Casts, Reddit, Shazam, Signal, Slack, Snapchat, SoundCloud, Spark, Spotify, Strava, Telegram, Things, Threads, TikTok, Tinder, Todoist, Trello, Tumblr, Twitch, X (Twitter), Uber, Uber Eats, Viber, Waze, WeChat, WhatsApp, YouTube, Zoom"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can create a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication"},{"type":"text","text":" with a resolved bundle ID, and use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication\/open(withAction:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication\/open(withActionHandler:)"},{"text":" to open it by triggering its deep link.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" enum doesn’t define certain apps that you need. You can ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"info@keyboardkit.com","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to add more apps to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/host-article"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Features","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Accessibility-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Actions-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AI-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/App-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Callouts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Clipboard-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Emojis-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/External-Keyboards-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Feedback-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Fonts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Gifs-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Layout-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Localization-Article"],"anchor":"Features"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"Feature-External.jpg":{"type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/src.KeyboardKit\/Feature-External.jpg"}],"alt":"Feature Icon","identifier":"Feature-External.jpg"},"doc://src.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/Features-Articles":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/features-articles","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Features","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","abstract"